Ms. Brannigan, this firm represents Ardsley Financial Group. Formal notice =
of claim is attached.<br />
<br />
Ardsley asserts that VAA interiors + architecture breached the professional=
 standard of care on project 632588 by specifying and issuing for construct=
ion a resilient flooring assembly with no moisture vapor mitigation over a =
lightweight concrete slab that the design team's own testing showed to be a=
t 92 to 96% relative humidity. The finish schedule issued under your firm's=
 seal, Revision 4 dated June 3, 2011, is the document Ardsley relied upon a=
nd it contains no mitigation system.<br />
<br />
Ardsley's damages to date total $2,150,000, comprising $1,180,000 in floori=
ng replacement, $412,000 in abatement and indoor air quality remediation, $=
398,000 in temporary relocation and business interruption, and $160,000 in =
consultant and testing costs.<br />
<br />
Please provide notice to your professional liability carrier and identify d=
efense counsel within twenty-one days.
